research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-6150-research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl:12:{"id":"lem-normal-sequences-of-entourages","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Iterated symmetric entourage roots are the standard normal-sequence construction in both sources, but the Statement makes the strictly weaker foundational hypothesis DC explicit and no located source states that same choice-calibrated proposition. It is established, not novel; the recursion proof is local. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: Iterating symmetric entourage roots to obtain a decreasing normal sequence with triple-composite control is the classical uniform-space construction. Exposing DC as the recursion principle is a foundational calibration of that standard result, not a novel claim.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-6151-research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl:13:{"id":"lem-pseudometric-from-a-normal-entourage-sequence","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"Both sources state the normal-sequence metrization lemma with the same dyadic control inclusions and path-infimum pseudometric construction. The proof is a notation-adjusted expansion.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-6152-research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl:14:{"id":"thm-entourage-uniformities-are-generated-by-gauges","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The sources prove every uniformity is generated by pseudometrics but assume an ordinary classical background; the item isolates DC as sufficient. The theorem is standard, but no source with the same foundational hypothesis surfaced. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: Representation of an arbitrary uniformity by a family of pseudometrics is a standard uniform-space theorem, and the current proof follows the usual normal-sequence construction. Stating DC as sufficient is an explicit choice calibration, so the local form is established and ai-altered.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
--
