research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7754-thm-uniformity-induces-a-topology 35:[A1] Entourages contain the diagonal, are closed under finite intersection, and have symmetric square roots ([[def-uniform-space-by-entourages]], [[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7755-thm-separated-uniformity-iff-induced-topology-is-hausdorff 37:[L1] Entourage balls are neighbourhood bases, and symmetric square roots exist ([[thm-uniformity-induces-a-topology]], [[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log:7756:lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary 30:[L1] Symmetric entourages form a base and have symmetric square roots ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]], [[def-uniform-space-by-entourages]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7757-lem-normal-sequences-of-entourages 35:[L1] Every entourage has a symmetric square root ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7758-lem-cauchy-filter-with-a-cluster-point-converges 32:[L2] Cauchy filters have small members, and symmetric entourages have symmetric square roots ([[def-cauchy-filter-in-a-uniform-space]], [[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7759-lem-minimal-cauchy-filter-associated-to-a-cauchy-filter 39:[L3] Symmetric entourages form a base ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7760-lem-entourages-on-minimal-cauchy-filters-form-a-separated-uniformity 37:[L2] Symmetric entourages form a base and admit square roots ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7764-thm-uniform-completion-universal-property-and-uniqueness 39:[L3] The basic entourages of $X_c$ declare two minimal Cauchy filters close when they have cross-close members ([[lem-entourages-on-minimal-cauchy-filters-form-a-separated-uniformity]]), and symmetric entourages with prescribed finite-composite control exist ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7765-lem-ultrafilters-on-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-cauchy 38:[L4] Every entourage contains a symmetric entourage whose square lies in it ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7766-lem-compact-uniform-spaces-are-totally-bounded 32:[L1] Symmetric entourages form a base ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7767-thm-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-unique-compatible-uniformity 36:[L4] Entourage balls form neighbourhood bases, symmetric entourages have square roots, and compactness supplies finite subcovers ([[thm-uniformity-induces-a-topology]], [[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]], [[def-compact-space]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log:7768:cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous 34:[L3] Every open cover of a nonempty compact Hausdorff space is uniform ([[thm-compact-hausdorff-open-cover-uniformity]]), and every uniform cover has an entourage-ball cover refining it ([[lem-entourage-and-uniform-cover-dictionary]]); every target entourage has a symmetric square root ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7769-lem-countable-uniform-base-normalisation 32:[L1] Symmetric entourages form a base and have square roots ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-a4-recovery.log-7770-lem-uniformizable-spaces-are-regular 39:[L3] Symmetric entourages have square roots, and a point is outside the closure of a set when it has a neighbourhood disjoint from that set ([[lem-symmetric-entourages-form-a-base]], [[def-interior-closure-boundary-top]]).
