research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-apply.log-166523- For a cover $\mathcal V$ of $X$ and $A\subseteq X$, write $\operatorname{St}(A,\mathcal V)$ for the union of the members of $\mathcal V$ meeting $A$. A cover $\mathcal V$ **star-refines** $\mathcal W$ if for every $V\in\mathcal V$, $\operatorname{St}(V,\mathcal V)$ is contained in some member of $\mathcal W$.
