research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-apply.log-176022-+1.1 For each continuous $f:X\to[0,1]$, direct substitution in [L4] shows that $p_f(x,y)=|f(x)-f(y)|$ is nonnegative, symmetric, zero on the diagonal and satisfies the triangle inequality, so it is a pseudometric; its balls about $x$ are original-open by [L2]. [L2, L4, construct]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-apply.log-176023- 
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform-apply.log-176024- 1.2 Conversely, if $x\in U$ is original-open, apply [L1] to the closed set $X\setminus U$ to obtain $f$ with $f(x)=1$ and $f[X\setminus U]=\{0\}$; then the $p_f$-ball of radius $1/2$ about $x$ lies in $U$. [L1, L3, choose]
